(5493637, 792193, 53316, '<td valign="top">I love this image!!! The colors are great and I really really like the lighting. Very unique and has a BIG visual impact.</td>', 'I love this image!!! The colors are great and I really really like the lighting. Very unique and has a BIG visual impact.', '2009-05-20 06:59:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493648, 792288, 28801, '<td valign="top">Nice composition. Focus does not appear to be on the near eye.</td>', 'Nice composition. Focus does not appear to be on the near eye.', '2009-05-20 07:06:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493662, 792110, 28801, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait, nice colours. That metal object in the upper right hand corner is driving me NUTS.</td>', 'Nice portrait, nice colours. That metal object in the upper right hand corner is driving me NUTS.', '2009-05-20 07:22:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493664, 792193, 28801, '<td valign="top">Near perfect shot ruined by distracting black bars</td>', 'Near perfect shot ruined by distracting black bars', '2009-05-20 07:24:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493666, 792072, 67152, '<td valign="top">pretty model but i notice severe pixelation issues in the image</td>', 'pretty model but i notice severe pixelation issues in the image', '2009-05-20 07:28:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493670, 792196, 51538, '<td valign="top">(The frame is really overdone).  I like the composition and colours, does the job.</td>', '(The frame is really overdone).  I like the composition and colours, does the job.', '2009-05-20 07:35:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493684, 792337, 53147, '<td valign="top">Did a quick vote of 20% to make sure my vote sticks with this one. Lovely image.</td>', 'Did a quick vote of 20% to make sure my vote sticks with this one. Lovely image.', '2009-05-20 08:04:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493686, 792266, 103032, '<td valign="top">I think the way you composed the model and cropped/framed the image is fine.  The lighting is good, but maybe a touch harsh.  Focus is right on; her eyes are captivating.  The negative aspect is the shelf(?) in the background.  It unnecessarily draws away from the model, which is a great glam shot.  Just my honest critique.</td>', 'I think the way you composed the model and cropped/framed the image is fine.  The lighting is good, but maybe a touch harsh.  Focus is right on; her eyes are captivating.  The negative aspect is the shelf(?) in the background.  It unnecessarily draws away from the model, which is a great glam shot.  Just my honest critique.', '2009-05-20 08:05:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493708, 791999, 103032, '<td valign="top">Well, the model certainly looks glamourous, but somehow the image isn''t "all there" as a package.  The focus and lighting are pretty good.  I guess the thing that throws me off is how exactly are you trying to work the cherries into the "glam" image???  I see just the tips of her fingers and part of the left cherry is cut off; both of which is distracting from the glam concept.  I''m thinking maybe you could have included more of her hand and all of the cherries.  Also, the cherry is "just" against her lip.  Maybe a more "seductive" (adding to the glam concept) way to incorporate the cherries (or maybe just one cherry would have been better) was to have the model pucker her lips against the cherry?  The photo just seems to be missing something...  But what do I know, its just my honest thoughts about the image...<br/> <br/>Looking at it some more, I do like the way you posed the model to look off to her side.  It gives the impression that the viewer was just "caught" looking at the subject; which is a nice technique.</td>', 'Well, the model certainly looks glamourous, but somehow the image isn''t "all there" as a package.  The focus and lighting are pretty good.  I guess the thing that throws me off is how exactly are you trying to work the cherries into the "glam" image???  I see just the tips of her fingers and part of the left cherry is cut off; both of which is distracting from the glam concept.  I''m thinking maybe you could have included more of her hand and all of the cherries.  Also, the cherry is "just" against her lip.  Maybe a more "seductive" (adding to the glam concept) way to incorporate the cherries (or maybe just one cherry would have been better) was to have the model pucker her lips against the cherry?  The photo just seems to be missing something...  But what do I know, its just my honest thoughts about the image... Looking at it some more, I do like the way you posed the model to look off to her side.  It gives the impression that the viewer was just "caught" looking at the subject; which is a nice technique.', '2009-05-20 08:28:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5493769, 792192, 106965, '<td valign="top">great hat.</td>', 'great hat.', '2009-05-20 09:23:26.000000', NULL, 1),
