(5501961, 792266, 48546, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MattO:</b></div><hr/><i> I have to admit, when I saw this image I was blown away that it was on the front page. With how picky and anal the voters are, to put this image on the front page with the distraction in the background just boggles my mind. The model is beautiful, it has great lighting on her, but that background literally kills what could have been a really great image. Congrats on the ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes it is truly mind-boggling.<br/> <br/>Ya know, I really agree that the shelf is a distraction. I say that up in the Photographer''s Comments. I would rather NOT have had the shelf in the shot. But yet, there it is. And for some reason, voters liked the shot anyway. Go figure.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-27 11:56:30.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by MattO: I have to admit, when I saw this image I was blown away that it was on the front page. With how picky and anal the voters are, to put this image on the front page with the distraction in the background just boggles my mind. The model is beautiful, it has great lighting on her, but that background literally kills what could have been a really great image. Congrats on the ribbon.   Yes it is truly mind-boggling. Ya know, I really agree that the shelf is a distraction. I say that up in the Photographer''s Comments. I would rather NOT have had the shelf in the shot. But yet, there it is. And for some reason, voters liked the shot anyway. Go figure.', '2009-05-27 11:24:42.000000', '2009-05-27 12:56:30.000000', 0),
